BASE KPIs:
-----------
1. Total Sales =  The sum of Unit Price , deducting the refunded value on return of items.
2. Unit Sold =  Number of item sold, tracks volume/demand size.
3. Total order =  This is the count of unique Order ID, tracks transaction volume/basket count.
4. Total Customers = Summation of Total Unique customers, to check the brand value of the product.
5. Cost/Unit = The average cost per product, required to check the expenditure of the company and manage cost for future transactions.
6. Total Returns = It the summation of the Amount refunded to the customer's account on return. Use to analyse the quality of the product or customer behaviour.
7. Total Products = To check the number of unique products bought.
8. Campaign Budget = To understand the total amount spent on campaigns and how they contribute to the revenue.
9. Campaing Count = Number of campaing for the products which helps us understand the amount spent on them and their usability.

PRIOR PERIOD KPIs:
------------------
1. Previous Month(PM) Sales, Unit Sold, Orders,Customers, Returns.
2. CM Vs. Monthly Sales Comparison =  CM (Current Month), this KPI is to compare the sales of the latest month with that of the previous months, to check the level of improvement business.
3. PM Budget, CAC(Customer Aquisition Cost), PM Campaign Add-to-Cart, PM Cost/Unit, PM CPC.

GROWTH & VARIANCE KPIs:
-----------------------
1. Running Totals / Cumulative Amount =  Total Sales made, Orders acquired, Unit sold by the company till date. Used to imply the overall growth of business.
2. MOM %(Month Over Month) = This is the monthly growth of sales, orders , unit sold, customers acquired , campaign budget variance to check the performance of business on a monthly basis.
3. Growth Segments Classifier = Rule-Based Categorisation (High growth, Fair Growth, Stable growth or Declining)

VENDOR & MARKETING KPIs:
------------------------
1. Excess Unit Sold = This is the extra amount of unit sold beyond the set threshold by the vendors.
2. Total Volume Discount % = This is the deduction in cost paid to the vendors as per the cost/unit on the excess amount of products sold on the particular month.
3. Cost Price = This is the total cost paid by the company on the number of products bought.
4. Net Payable to Vendors = This the cost paid by the company after the discount for the next purchase.
5.Total CPC =  This means Total Cost per clicks, which helps us identify the intensity of expenditure made a campaign for drawing customers. The lesser the CPC the better.
6.Add-to-Cart % = This the number of items added to cart after clicking on the ad-campaign, shows how many people are interested to buy the product.
7.Cart Conversion Rate % = To check how many items which were added to cart were ordered.
8.Click-Through-% = To check how many people were interested on viewing the ad.
9.Conversion % = To see the ratio of interested customer to the customers who bought the product , this is an important metrics to check the quality of campaign and demand of the product.
10.Return-On-AdSepnd = This is percentage of sales made on spending on a campaign. Ideally it should always be more than 100%.




